course: dictionary
lesson: 9850
title: One name, different trees
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A word can mean different things in different places. The sycamore is a good example. In Britain and Ireland, «sycamore seeds» are the winged seeds of a large maple tree with five-pointed leaves. Those seeds spin as they fall, which is why children call them «sycamore helicopters».
explain: «Sycamore helicopters spin down slowly so the wind can carry them away.» The spinning slows the fall, so the wind has time to take each seed away from the parent tree. This is one way that seeds are spread to new places.
explain: In North America, a sycamore is a tall plane tree with bark that peels off in patches of white, green and brown. In the Bible story of Zacchaeus, a short man climbs a sycamore fig tree to see Jesus. So when you read the word, look at the clues around it to find out which tree is meant.
fact: A sycamore is a type of tree, and its name can mean different trees in different places.
fact: «Sycamore seeds» have a wing that makes them spin as they fall, like little helicopters.
fact: The pale wood of the sycamore is used for furniture and kitchen spoons.
fact: In Britain and Ireland, a sycamore is a large maple; in the USA and Canada, it is a tall plane tree.
fact: Context check: a sentence about spinning seeds means the maple-type tree, and a sentence about Zacchaeus means a fig tree.
exercise: What makes «sycamore seeds» spin as they fall? | Their heavy roots | Their sweet smell | *A wing | A long tail
exercise: In which kind of text does a short man climb a sycamore to see Jesus? | *A Bible story | A map of London | A science report | A cookery book
exercise: What is the pale sycamore wood used for? | Paper plates only | Making steel pipes | Building roads | *Furniture and kitchen spoons
test: What slows a sycamore seed's fall? | *It spins like a helicopter | It sinks in water | It falls straight like a stone | It floats on a fluffy parachute
test: In Britain, what kind of tree is a sycamore? | A pine tree | *A maple | A willow | A fig tree
exam: Ruby reads, in an American book, «a tall plane tree with bark that peels off in patches». Which tree is the sycamore here? | A fig tree in the Middle East | A tree that grows pale wood for spoons | A maple with five-pointed leaves | *A tall plane tree
